## Use the area with PQ as the base
Area $= \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{perpendicular height}$, with area $16\sqrt{3}$ and base $8$.
16\sqrt{3} &= \frac{1}{2} \times 8 \times h
16\sqrt{3} &= 4h
## Divide both sides by 4
h &= \frac{16\sqrt{3}}{4}
h &= 4\sqrt{3} \text{ cm}
ANSWER: 4\sqrt{3} \text{ cm}

## (i) Probability the first animal is a cat
There are 14 cats out of 40 animals.
P(\text{cat}) &= \frac{14}{40}
&= \frac{7}{20}
## (ii) Probability that all three are male dogs
There are 11 male dogs. Each animal picked is not replaced, so both numbers drop by 1 each time.
P(\text{3 male dogs}) &= \frac{11}{40} \times \frac{10}{39} \times \frac{9}{38}
&= \frac{33}{1976}
&\approx 0.017
ANSWER: \text{(i) } \frac{7}{20} \qquad \text{(ii) } 0.017

## Find the height x of the removed top cone
The small cone on top is similar to the whole cone, so corresponding sides are in the same ratio.
\frac{3}{7.5} &= \frac{x}{47}
x &= \frac{3 \times 47}{7.5}
x &= 18.8
## Subtract from the full height
k &= 47 - 18.8
k &= 28.2
ANSWER: k = 28.2 \text{ m}

## Divide to find the length of 1 nautical mile
27 nautical miles equal 50 km, so divide 50 km by 27.
1 \text{ nautical mile} &= \frac{50}{27} \text{ km}
&\approx 1.852 \text{ km}
ANSWER: 1.852 \text{ km}

## Set up the tangent ratio
49 m is opposite the angle and $d$ is adjacent. At first, $d$ is in metres.
\tan 1.2^\circ &= \frac{49}{d}
d &= \frac{49}{\tan 1.2^\circ}
d &\approx 2339.2 \text{ m}
## Convert metres to kilometres
d &= \frac{2339.2}{1000}
d &\approx 2.34 \text{ km}
ANSWER: d = 2.34 \text{ km}

## Set up Pythagoras on half of the roof triangle
The roof height is $8.5 - 7 = 1.5$ m and half the width is $12 \div 2 = 6$ m. $d$ is the hypotenuse.
d^2 &= 6^2 + 1.5^2
d^2 &= 36 + 2.25
d^2 &= 38.25
## Take the square root
d &= \sqrt{38.25}
d &\approx 6.18465
d &\approx 6.2 \text{ m}
ANSWER: d = 6.2 \text{ m}

## Use the sine rule
The side $|AB| = 3$ is opposite angle $C$. The side $|BC| = 4.65$ is opposite the $30^\circ$ angle.
\frac{\sin C}{3} &= \frac{\sin 30^\circ}{4.65}
\sin C &= \frac{3 \sin 30^\circ}{4.65}
\sin C &= \frac{1.5}{4.65}
\sin C &= \frac{10}{31}
## Take the inverse sine
C &= \sin^{-1}\left(\frac{10}{31}\right)
C &\approx 18.819063^\circ
C &\approx 19^\circ
ANSWER: |\angle ACB| = 19^\circ

## Cross-multiply to remove the fractions
\frac{1}{h} &= \frac{k}{j+k}
j + k &= hk
## Collect the terms in k on one side
k - hk &= -j
## Factorise out k
k(1 - h) &= -j
## Divide both sides by 1 − h
k &= -\frac{j}{1-h}
k &= \frac{j}{h-1}
ANSWER: k = \frac{j}{h-1}
